Import or export data to a PostgreSQL database, scripts must be run from this
directory.

Environment variables used by scripts:

  PGHOST/PGPORT/PGUSER/...: used by the psql command
  SQLITE3: sqlite3 command to use

./import.sh <database> [<typeschema>] <schema> [drop]

Import SCOWL data into PostgreSQL.

<database> is the PostgreSQL database.

<schema> is the schema to import the data into.  If the schema doesn't exist
it will be created.  If the schema exists than all tables are truncated.  If
'drop' is specified first attempt to drop the schema so it can be recreated.

<typeschema> is the schema for enums used by the database.  It defaults to
<schema> if omitted.  If the schema doesn't exists than it will be created and
populated.  The 'drop' option will not drop <typeschema>.

The env. var. SCOWL_DB can be used to set the sqlite3 db file, otherwise it
defaults to '../scowl.db'

./export.sh <database> <schema> <sqlite-db-file>

Export SCOWL data from PostgreSQL.

